# Documentation: 13-uploads.http REST client collection.
# - Covers avatar and product image uploads against the R2-backed upload endpoints.
# - These requests require a working bucket binding, `R2_PUBLIC_URL`, and the sample fixture path declared in the multipart body.
# - These requests are written for the VS Code REST Client extension and use its response-variable syntax extensively.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8787
@seedPassword = Test@1234
@adminEmail = admin.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test

### These requests require:
### - a working R2 bucket binding
### - R2_PUBLIC_URL configured for local dev
### - the bundled 1x1 PNG fixture below

# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### Upload avatar image
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=RestClientBoundary

--RestClientBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="1x1.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/1x1.png
--RestClientBoundary--

### Upload product photo
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/product-photo
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=RestClientBoundary

--RestClientBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="1x1.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/1x1.png
--RestClientBoundary--
